{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/498550-multitribe-packs-how-do-they-function","id":498550,"title":"Multitribe packs-how do they function?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-01T02:30:22-07:00","id":498550,"title":"Multitribe packs-how do they function?","content":"so i just got the advance pdf of second ed and i'm a bit fuzzy on how multitribal packs work. each tribe has its own sacred prey and gets testy if a werewolf from another tribe gets into their kool-aid. So are multitribe packs common? how do they work with each other if half the pack is not supposed to hunt the prey? can they all participate in the sacred hunt or is that frowned upon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5767-deedee","name":"DeeDee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T02:44:51-07:00","id":498572,"title":"","content":"I think multi-tribal Packs are very common... Nearly every game I've seen tends to want one Uratha from each tribe going in. I understand the concern of a specific prey being that Tribe's thing. I would solve it (having not actually played a game as of yet I can only put forth opinion) that whilst the Pack goes on the hunt and they all have parts to play, when it comes to the killing blow or ending the hunt, that tribe's Uratha 'takes the kill', so to speak. I think a good ST would work it so that hunts revolve and different prey come up to have each tribe's Uratha have a moment in the limelight.<br /> That's my opinion anyway. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T02:45:22-07:00","id":498574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeeDee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/498550-multitribe-packs-how-do-they-function#post498550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">each tribe has its own sacred prey and gets testy if a werewolf from another tribe gets into their kool-aid</div> </div> </div> </div>Effectively it works because what I quoted is wrong. Tribes have their sacred prey, and they view that prey add important to hunt, but not important that only they hunt it. <br /> <br /> Multitribe packs are the norm for parties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5292-flailbot","name":"FlailBot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T02:49:52-07:00","id":498578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeeDee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/498550-multitribe-packs-how-do-they-function#post498550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">how do they work with each other if half the pack is not supposed to hunt the prey?</div> </div> </div> </div>The quoted text is inaccurate - members of Tribes that do not have a given prey as their favoured, focused prey are still perfectly allowed to hunt said prey.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T07:26:16-07:00","id":498812,"title":"","content":"Favored prey is just that. Favorite. Just because my favorite food is corned beef and my friend's favorite food is spaghetti doesn't mean he can't eat corned beef or I can't eat spaghetti.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T07:46:29-07:00","id":498828,"title":"","content":"No Spaghetti for you... One Year...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T07:52:55-07:00","id":498833,"title":"","content":"Well, it does encourage a diversity of tactics within the Pack, so that they can handle more threats. At the same time, it allows characters to drive the story, both by delineating the Pack's options in a given situation, and by providing potential blind spots for the ST to exploit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T09:10:53-07:00","id":498983,"title":"","content":"The advantages of multi-tribal packs versus those of single-tribe packs are very much comprable to the tension of specialization or diversity in character creation. Do you want to be able to function adequately in any given situation, or do you want to be <i>really good</i> at one thing at the cost of being disadvantaged in some other situations? You could make a pack of all Bone Shadows and be amazing at hunting spirits, but you'll have a harder time fighting against the Pure or protecting your territory against Hosts. Alternatively, you could have one member of each Tribe in a pack, and then no matter your prey you'd have someone who could take the lead and know how to handle that foe, but the Pack won't have as much unity of purpose or be as effective at fighting any given prey.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T14:20:02-07:00","id":499385,"title":"","content":"But are you really having a &quot;harder time&quot; hunting things not your specialized Prey. I don't really see that. You may not have some nice tricks up your sleeve (really, those tricks are not really all that required, right), but you are still a pack of werewolves, and not much stands against a unified pack of werewolves for very long, in my experience. Especially if they have some experience under their belts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T15:04:14-07:00","id":499425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/498550-multitribe-packs-how-do-they-function?p=499385#post499385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But are you really having a &quot;harder time&quot; hunting things not your specialized Prey. I don't really see that.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think it's pretty clearly represented in the advantages of each tribe's Siskur Dah. Storm Lords can straight up identify the Claimed by looking at them. How does that not make things easier?<br /> <br /> Not to mention that your prey being favoured means you are more experienced at facing them. Your skills and knowledge would likely reflect that. An Irraka Bone Shadow, for example is more likely to have enough Occult knowledge to track or predict a spirit's movements and behaviours, likewise a Bone Shadow Rahu may have the Spiritual Blockage merit, which can be incredibly useful in fighting spirits. An Elodoth Iron Master is more likely to have the urban connections and Streetwise to entrap an otherwise well protected Mafia boss. I could go on.<br /> <br /> No pack's territory is going to have just one kind of enemy in it, so yes, a Tribe of Blood Talons might wish they had an Iron Master in their ranks when it comes to dealing with ousting a corrupt politician (who may also be a vampire) causing damage to their territory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","user":"Amravanti","date":". 05-01-2015, 06:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T16:04:42-07:00","id":499470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/498550-multitribe-packs-how-do-they-function?p=499385#post499385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But are you really having a &amp;quot;harder time&amp;quot; hunting things not your specialized Prey. I don't really see that. You may not have some nice tricks up your sleeve (really, those tricks are not really all that required, right), but you are still a pack of werewolves, and not much stands against a unified pack of werewolves for very long, in my experience. Especially if they have some experience under their belts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it easier to hunt your favored prey or harder to hunt everything else? Six of one and half-a-dozen of the other, really. Just depends how you want to parse it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T16:17:30-07:00","id":499474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/498550-multitribe-packs-how-do-they-function?p=499385#post499385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But are you really having a &quot;harder time&quot; hunting things not your specialized Prey. I don't really see that. You may not have some nice tricks up your sleeve (really, those tricks are not really all that required, right), but you are still a pack of werewolves, and not much stands against a unified pack of werewolves for very long, in my experience. Especially if they have some experience under their belts.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Harder&quot; is not the same thing as &quot;hard&quot;. Siskur-Dah aside, you get a +2 to activating Facets when facing your Tribe's sacred prey. If everyone in the pack has the same sacred prey and that's the thing you're fighting, then you will have an easier time with it. If only one amongst you has that benefit, then you wll have a harder time with it. This is slight, but its necessarily true.<br /> On top of that, you probably have the benefits Amravanti mentioned. If you built your characters around Tribal concepts, then more than just the inate Tribal benefits will be focused on your Tribe's sacred prey. If a pack has five wolves built five different ways, then at any given time, four of them will not be maximum effectiveness. Sure, werewolves are a generally effective lot, but a group where everyone is at the top of their game when facing a particular foe will have an edge over one where just one amongst them is perfectly suited to the task.<br /> <br /> Siskur-Dah, on the other hand, is something of an equalizer. You perform it, and your whole pack gets an edge over your Tribe's sacred prey. It's not about what Tribe the individual is in when you're on the Siskur-Dah, it's about the Tribe of the one who performed the Rite. Thus, if your pack will be facing more than one of the various Tribes' sacred prey (which every pack invariably will), it's really helpful to have people from several different Tribes in your pack to get your hunt rolling. Once the hunt is on, everyone has an edge over that prey. Sure, not the inate +2 or the bonuses from the build, but the benefit from the Rite itself is no joke.<br /> <br /> The long and the short of this is that every Tribe has tools to deal with its own prey. Having multiple Tribes gives your pack tools to hunt most things that might come your way. Having multiple Uratha from one Tribe will make that Tribe's prey even easier to handle. Being without a Tribe gives your pack a blind-spot. <br /> The basic unit of werewolf life is the pack. If you see a threat to your territory, you're not going to tell your pack-mates that you're going to handle it alone just because it's your Tribe's favorite prey and not theirs. That would be foolhardy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T19:49:49-07:00","id":499677,"title":"","content":"I think multi tribal packs are the exception, not necessarily the rule. Up until max roman started pushing it heavily after the fall of gurdilag I think most packs were inter tribal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T12:48:29-07:00","id":500640,"title":"","content":"I've only read so much of the fiction (the Idigam Chronicle Anthology and the stuff in the 2E book), so I don't know what's supposed to be the cannon history for Uratha (or if there is supposed to be one), but here's the way I see it:<br /> <br /> In a pack, you have a totem, and that totem spirit grows as the pack grows and the Uratha in it uphold it more.<br /> In a Tribe, you have a First-born, who is super strong and the patron of a world-wide group of Uratha.<br /> Somewhere in the middle, you have lodges that have a lot of Werewolves in them and moderately well-endowed spirit heads.<br /> <br /> In effect, all three tiers are the same thing: one spiritual leader at the top of a pile of Werewolves, granting them all a boon and feeding off their loyalty. There are some lodges who's ideologies align so much with a Tribe that they demand it for membership, but there are also ones who's unifying feature has so little to do with Tribal ethos that any tribe can join it. Similarly, if your pack wants to focus on one thing, maybe it makes sense for them all to be from one Tribe. But if that one thing is &quot;anything that's happening in our territory&quot;, then that could overlap with any Tribe and there's no reason not to have different viewpoints represented.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T12:57:16-07:00","id":500645,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't consider the totem the 'leader' of the pack, outside of the Pure. Even the lodge totems. They are more like mentors and liaisons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-02-2015, 04:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T15:26:28-07:00","id":500845,"title":"","content":"I think nofather is right. They get w mutual relationship, not leadership.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}